ce", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-20", "plays": 543, "likes": 16, "comments": 0}], "still_climbing": false, "transcript": "I cleaned the house before the cleaner came. I know how that sounds. I nearly canceled my first clean, an hour before. I was that close. It's a stranger in your house, going through your things. That felt like a lot. And I was embarrassed, which is stupid. That's literally why you hire someone. So for the first while, I just followed her around, asking if she needed anything, checking on her. And then eventually, I made myself a coffee and sat down. And that was it. I stopped watching. She finished, showed me each room, and I remember going quiet. Not because it was clean, but because it was done and I hadn't done it. By the time she left, I was completely relaxed, joking with her at the door. Nothing like the person who apologized to her three hours earlier.", "is_relevant": true, "hook_type": "Personal Experience"}, {"shortCode": "DdWgfLfGeHi", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DdWgfLfGeHi/", "caption": "I didn\u2019t realize how much of my stress was coming from my house.\n\nIt wasn\u2019t just the cleaning \u2014 it was constantly noticing everything that still needed to be done.\n\nNow I can actually sit in my own home without mentally adding things to a to-do list.\n\n\ud83d\udccd Montreal\nGet your quote through the link in bio.\n\n#montreal #HomeCleaning #housecleaning #homecleaning #montrealmoms", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T14:32:44.000Z", "videoDuration": 24.70458, "videoPlayCount": 556, "videoViewCount": null, "likesCount": 17, "commentsCount": 0, "displayUrl": "https://scontent-ham3-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/808645030_17909659320540209_3580426660509169665_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e15_tt6&_nc_cat=105&ig_cache_key=Mzk4NzUxNzQwMDIwODIzNzAyNjE3OTA5NjU5MzE3NTQwMjA5.3-ccb7-5&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=58cdad&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6IkNMSVBTLnhwaWRzLjEwODAuc2RyLnZpZGVvX2RlZmF1bHRfY292ZXJfZnJhbWUuQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=p_-2SzViL1wQ7kNvwEEQ0F8&_nc_oc=Ad